#!/usr/bin/env python3
# veron -- the stage 5 driver.
#
# ONE SCRIPT, TWO ENVIRONMENTS. The runner and a laptop run the identical
# thing. The workflow is a caller: checkout, airlock, `veron ...`. If build
# logic appears in YAML again, that is the regression this file exists to
# prevent, and `tools/lint-workflow` is what catches it.
#
# THE PLAN IS THE CONTRACT. Nothing executes that was not printed first.
# `veron plan` expands every step to literal argv -- no shell, no implicit
# template, no defaults applied at run time that were not visible at plan
# time. `veron build` executes exactly that, in order, logging each argv and
# its return code.
#
# Python 3.11+ (tomllib). Standard library only, deliberately: this is a host
# orchestrator in the airlock, tier 2 like bubblewrap, and it must never
# acquire a dependency that could reach the artifact path.

